  {%- endcomment -%}
  .itm-pg-picker__name {
    padding-right: 8px;
    font-family: var(--font-heading-family);
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: #131313;
    text-decoration: none;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }
  .itm-pg-picker__name:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
  {%- comment -%}
    overflow: hidden + break-word — some scraped spec values come through
    as one run-on word with no spaces at all (a mis-parsed multi-value
    field, e.g. "FlipReverseLever"), which white-space: normal can't wrap
    on its own since there's no space to break at. Without this it just
    overflowed its 150px box and visibly bled into whatever sat next to it
    — including, at the far end of a row, the sticky Price/Add to Cart
    zone.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  .itm-pg-picker__cell {
    flex: 0 0 150px;
    min-width: 0;
    max-width: 150px;
    overflow: hidden;
    overflow-wrap: break-word;
    word-break: break-word;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    padding: 12px 0;
    font-size: 13px;
    line-height: 1.35;
    color: #444444;
